#italic#

I am happy to announce Forbidden Cults the third expansion to Tales of Maj'Eyal!
It works just like Ashes of Urh'rok, adding new and *wonderful* stuff to the base game instead of a new campaign like Embers of Rage did, but adding more!

So what does Forbidden Cults add you will ask? Take a look:
* Play as a Writhing One class: give in to the corrupting forces and turn yourself gradually into an horror, summon horrors to do your bidding, shed your skin and melt your face to assault your foes. With your arm already turned into tentacle, what creature can stop you?
* Unlock the Cultist of Entropy class: using its insanity and control of entropic forces to unravel the normal laws of physic this caster class can turn healing into attacks and call upon the forces of the void to reduce its foes to dust
* Unlock the Drem race: a corrupt subrace of dwarves that somehow managed to keep its own mind and not fully devolve into a mindless horror
* Unlock the Krog race: a ogre transformed by the very thing that should kill them
* Start in your "hometown" of Kroshkkur, an ancient Sher'tul Fortress laying half in ruins that serves as a focal point, and home for all kinds of creatures seeking lost knowledge
* Discover a new resource: Insanity, used by both new classes, that gradually makes you more chaotic and powerful as it fills up
* Play through the starting zone The Maggot, a huge living corrupted worm about to destroy Kroshkkur!
* Discover two other horrific zones along with their not so friendly inhabitants
* Find and read the Forbidden Tomes... if you dare
* Unearth the secrets of ancient glyphs and the Occult Egress
- Unlock the S.M.A.C.K. feature for the Fortress, letting you battle AI-controlled clones of other people's characters currently online!
- Unlock a new drake tree for Wyrmics
- Learn more about the old ages of Eyal and the Gods
- Earn new achievements (because Tales of Maj'Eyal does not have enough!)
- Find new artifacts
- New custom made graphics and musics

Now sit back and relax while the shadows move in the background, slowly slithing their way up to you.
